|  Digital Research C READ.ME File Notes	        May 1984 |
|								 |
|								 |
|	13. A  minimum   192K   of  random  access  memory  is	 |
|	    recommended to operate the C compiler.		 |
|								 |
|	14. The command line example for  reverse preprocessor	 |
|	    operation on page 2-16 of the  Programmer's  Guide	 |
|	    should read as follows.				 |
|								 |
|	    	B>DRC CTEMP.TOK					 |
|								 |
|	15. Note that the __BDOS function  described  on  page   |
|	    3-4  of  the  Programmer's  Guide  uses a "double"	 |
|	    underscore character.  It is easy  to  mistake  it	 |
|	    for a single underscore.				 |
|								 |
|	16. The first line  of the sample program, OVERLAY1.C,	 |
|	    on page 7-3 of the  Programmer's  Guide  does  not	 |
|	    need the semi-colon.   The  line  should  read  as	 |
|	    follows:  overlay1(s)				 |
|								 |
|	17. Note that the compiler command line options -R and	 |
|	    -A described in Section 2.1.3  of the Programmer's	 |
|	    Guide are mutually exclusive.    This  means  that	 |
|	    when  you  specify  one  option,    the  other  is	 |
|	    automatically canceled.				 |
|								 |
|	18. There  is  an  additional  compiler  command  line	 |
|	    option that is not documented in the  Programmer's	 |
|	    Guide.  The -4  option  directs  the  compiler  to	 |
|	    search a specified  drive  for  the  DRC.ERR file.	 |
|	    The following  example  directs  the  compiler  to	 |
|	    search drive d: for DRC.ERR.				 |
|								 |
|		B>DRC PROGRAM -4d:				 |
|								 |
|	19. There is a preferred procedure you must follow  if	 |
|	    you  encounter an  "Internal Compiler Error"  when	 |
|	    using Digital Research C.				 |
|								 |
|	    After determining how you  produced  the  internal	 |
|	    error, reproduce  the  error  in  a  small  sample	 |
|	    program.     Submit  the  sample  to  the  Digital	 |
|	    Research Technical Support Center by mail.  If the	 |
|	    sample is more than 10 lines long, submit the code	 |
|	    on diskette.					 |
|								 |
|				Page 4				 |
